<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Legal & Content Standards — Omnilore</title><meta name="description" content="Omnilore terms, privacy notice, content advisory, copyright policy, and accessibility statement."><link rel="icon" href="assets/logo.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,500&family=EB+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&display=swap"><style>:root{--ink:#030405;--paper:#eee6d3;--muted:#aaa69d;--brass:#e0c878;--cyan:#8bbfc1;--line:rgba(238,230,211,.15)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 83% 10%,rgba(139,191,193,.08),transparent 22%),var(--ink);color:var(--paper);font:18px/1.6 'EB Garamond',Georgia,serif}.nav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:3;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;height:68px;padding:0 clamp(18px,4vw,60px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);background:rgba(3,4,5,.94);backdrop-filter:blur(16px)}.nav img{width:30px}.brand{color:var(--paper);text-decoration:none;font:500 .55rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:2px}.brand strong{display:block;color:var(--brass);font:700 1.28rem 'Cormorant Garamond',serif;letter-spacing:.5px}.nav a:last-child{margin-left:auto;color:var(--cyan);font:500 .58rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-decoration:none;text-transform:uppercase}.hero{padding:95px max(22px,9vw) 64px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.eyebrow{color:var(--cyan);font:500 .58rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:3px;text-transform:uppercase}.hero h1{max-width:800px;margin:12px 0;font:700 clamp(3.5rem,8vw,7rem)/.84 'Cormorant Garamond',serif;letter-spacing:-2px}.hero p{max-width:650px;color:var(--muted)}.warning{max-width:1050px;margin:34px auto 0;padding:17px 20px;border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:rgba(224,200,120,.07);color:rgba(238,230,211,.74);font-size:.96rem}.layout{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:70px 24px 110px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px minmax(0,1fr);gap:65px}.toc{align-self:start;position:sticky;top:96px;border-left:1px solid var(--line);padding-left:16px}.toc a{display:block;margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--muted);font:500 .55rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:1px;text-decoration:none;text-transform:uppercase}.toc a:hover{color:var(--cyan)}article section{padding:0 0 48px;margin-bottom:48px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}article h2{margin:0 0 14px;font:700 clamp(2rem,4vw,3.3rem)/.9 'Cormorant Garamond',serif;letter-spacing:-1px}article h3{margin:26px 0 8px;color:var(--brass);font:600 1.25rem 'Cormorant Garamond',serif}article p,article li{color:rgba(238,230,211,.74)}article ul{padding-left:20px}.callout{padding:17px 20px;background:rgba(139,191,193,.08);border:1px solid rgba(139,191,193,.19);color:rgba(238,230,211,.78)}.missing{color:#f0c98d;font:500 .59rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.7px}footer{padding:45px 24px;text-align:center;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:rgba(238,230,211,.4);font:500 .54rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:1.5px}@media(max-width:760px){.layout{display:block;padding-top:45px}.toc{position:static;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 15px;margin-bottom:40px;border:0;padding:0}.toc a{margin:0}.hero{padding:72px 24px 50px}}</style></head><body><nav><img src="assets/logo.svg" alt="Omnilore seal"><a class="brand" href="index.html"><strong>Omnilore</strong>THE ARCHIVE OF ALL THINGS UNREAL</a><a href="index.html">Return to archive</a></nav><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Legal & content standards</p><h1>Read before you descend.</h1><p>These policies explain the rules of using Omnilore, the nature of its materials, and how to raise a concern. Last updated: July 25, 2026.</p><div class="warning"><strong>Important:</strong> This is a public-facing policy framework for a pre-launch, read-only archive. It must be reviewed and completed with a qualified lawyer before public launch, especially after a contact address, hosting provider, analytics, advertising, accounts, uploads, or paid services are added.</div></header><main class="layout"><nav class="toc" aria-label="Legal sections"><a href="#content-advisory">Content advisory</a><a href="#terms">Terms</a><a href="#privacy">Privacy</a><a href="#copyright">Copyright</a><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav><article><section id="content-advisory"><h2>Content advisory</h2><p>Omnilore documents mythology, folklore, religion, art, literature, horror, urban legends, internet folklore, and fictional worlds. Its entries may contain or link to material involving artistic or historical nudity; religious or occult imagery; demons; monsters; fictional violence or gore; death; body horror; disturbing themes; trauma; or language and perspectives that are historically dated, prejudicial, or offensive.</p><p>Material is organized for research, context, cataloguing, and cultural reference. Inclusion does not mean endorsement, approval, factual verification, or suitability for every audience. Use your own judgment before viewing an entry, following an external link, or conducting a search. Omnilore is not intended for children or for anyone who is not legally permitted to access this type of material where they live.</p></section><section id="terms"><h2>Terms of use</h2><h3>Agreement and eligibility</h3><p>By accessing Omnilore, you agree to these Terms and confirm that you are legally able to view the material in your location. If you do not agree, do not use the site.</p><h3>Archive purpose</h3><p>Omnilore is a read-only reference archive operated by Timothy Garcia. It currently provides informational and creative cataloguing only. It does not offer accounts, user uploads, comments, direct messaging, paid transactions, professional advice, or a guarantee that any entry is complete, current, accurate, safe, or appropriate for a particular purpose.</p><h3>Your choices and responsibility</h3><p>You control your searches, navigation, and decision to open an entry or external resource. You are responsible for complying with laws that apply to you and for using the archive appropriately. Omnilore does not promise to filter every possible sensitive result or to predict what any visitor may find upsetting.</p><h3>Permitted use</h3><p>You may browse, quote short portions with attribution where lawful, and use the archive for personal research, education, criticism, commentary, and other lawful purposes. You may not scrape at a harmful rate, bypass technical controls, misrepresent the archive as your own, use it to harass or harm others, or use any material in violation of applicable law or the rights of others.</p><h3>Disclaimers and limitation</h3><p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Omnilore is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot legally be excluded. This policy does not replace legal advice, and it does not excuse unlawful conduct by the operator or a visitor.</p></section><section id="privacy"><h2>Privacy notice</h2><p>Omnilore is currently a read-only static website. It does not currently offer accounts, comments, forms, newsletters, payments, user uploads, advertising, or intentionally configured analytics.</p><p>Like most websites, the hosting provider and a visitor’s browser may process technical information such as IP address, device/browser information, request time, and pages requested in order to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Omnilore also loads Google Fonts and may display source images or links hosted by third parties; those services may receive technical request information under their own policies.</p><p>Essential local storage is used only to remember that a visitor has acknowledged the content advisory. No sale of personal information is intended. If data practices change, this notice must be updated before the new feature goes live.</p><div class="callout"><span class="missing">PRE-LAUNCH REQUIREMENT:</span> Publish a working privacy/contact email and identify the hosting provider, all analytics, all advertising, and all third-party embeds before public launch.</div></section><section id="copyright"><h2>Copyright & takedown</h2><p>Names, stories, artwork, photographs, texts, trademarks, and other source materials may belong to their respective rights holders. Omnilore does not claim ownership of third-party materials except where expressly stated. Source-linked or reference material should be used only as permitted by law and by the rights holder’s terms.</p><p>If you believe material on Omnilore infringes your copyright or other rights, send a detailed notice identifying the work, the exact page or URL, your authority to act, your contact information, and a good-faith statement. Omnilore will review credible notices and may remove, correct, attribute, or otherwise address the material as appropriate.</p><p class="missing">LEGAL CONTACT EMAIL HAS NOT YET BEEN PROVIDED. A working copyright/contact address must be added before this site is made public.</p></section><section id="accessibility"><h2>Accessibility</h2><p>Omnilore aims to make the archive usable with keyboard navigation, readable contrast, responsive layouts, meaningful image alternatives where available, and reduced-motion support. Some historical source material or third-party images may not yet meet every accessibility expectation. If you find a barrier, report it through the legal/contact address once published.</p></section><section id="contact"><h2>Operator & contact</h2><p><strong>Operator:</strong> Timothy Garcia</p><p><strong>Archive:</strong> Omnilore — The Archive of All Things Unreal</p><p class="missing"><strong>Contact email:</strong> to be supplied and published before public launch.</p></section></article></main><footer>OMNILORE — THE ARCHIVE OF ALL THINGS UNREAL · LEGAL & CONTENT STANDARDS</footer></body></html>